          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>When two logarithmic terms in an expression have the same base and argument, we can combine them by adding their coefficients.</p>",
            "readable_text": "When two logarithmic terms in an expression have the same base and argument, we can combine them by adding their coefficients.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To demonstrate, let&#x27;s look at the expression\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5\\log_{\\color{blue}4}{\\color{red}7}+3\\log_{\\color{blue}4}{\\color{red}7}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "To demonstrate, let's look at the expression\n[MATH: 5\\log_{\\color{blue}4}{\\color{red}7}+3\\log_{\\color{blue}4}{\\color{red}7}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Both logarithmic terms have a base of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\color{blue}4]</span> and an argument of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{red}7}.]</span> Therefore, we can combine them by adding their coefficients:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Both logarithmic terms have a base of [MATH: \\color{blue}4] and an argument of [MATH: {\\color{red}7}.] Therefore, we can combine them by adding their coefficients:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5\\log_{4} 7 + 3\\log_{4} 7|= (5 + 3)\\log_{4} 7 = 8\\log_{4} 7]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 5\\log_{4} 7 + 3\\log_{4} 7|= (5 + 3)\\log_{4} 7 = 8\\log_{4} 7]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nWhen two logarithmic terms in an expression have the same base and argument, we can combine them by adding their coefficients.\n\nContent:\nTo demonstrate, let's look at the expression\n[MATH: 5\\log_{\\color{blue}4}{\\color{red}7}+3\\log_{\\color{blue}4}{\\color{red}7}.]\n\nContent:\nBoth logarithmic terms have a base of [MATH: \\color{blue}4] and an argument of [MATH: {\\color{red}7}.] Therefore, we can combine them by adding their coefficients:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 5\\log_{4} 7 + 3\\log_{4} 7|= (5 + 3)\\log_{4} 7 = 8\\log_{4} 7]"
      },
